    "habitat": "continental_slope",
    "order": 23,
    "notes": "Gelatinous sculpin: huge soft bulbous head, a droopy fleshy 'nose' over a wide down-turned mouth with fleshy lips, small eyes, fan-like pectoral fins and a short body tapering to a small tail; pinkish grey. The blob look is the famous surface (decompressed) look, kept for recognisability; alive it is a greyer tadpole-shaped fish. The nose is the snout box at the front of the head."
